# Harness preservation

Distributed clones must stay **predictable** without an owner watching every chat. Treat **shipped core** as behavior-frozen unless the operator clearly authorizes a harness behavior change.

## Shipped core (do not edit casually)

- Always-on rules: `communication.mdc`, `structure.mdc`, `documentation.mdc`, `hygiene.mdc`, `intent.mdc`, `delegation.mdc`, `preservation.mdc`
- Hook contract: `.cursor/hooks.json` events; PowerShell-only `.cursor/hooks/*.ps1`
- Inject protocol: read `inject-snapshot.json`, `docClose`, progressive L0→L1→L2 load in `l0.json`
- Canonical lists in `.cursor/docs/manifest.json`
- Slash **behavior** for: `onboarding`, `better-prompt`, `better-skill` (`better-prompt` / `better-skill` are Conversation coaches only; no execution)
- `operator-assist.json` → `betterPrompt.version` and `betterSkill.version` coach contracts (bump only with intentional release)

## Allowed without behavioral entrust

- Task work under allowlist (e.g. harness templates, user stack under `.cursor/harness/`)
- Tier content outside shipped core when the task requires it
- `README.md` / `AGENTS.md` when the operator explicitly requests
- Bugfixes that **restore** documented behavior (typo, broken path, `verify-harness` failure)
- Doc sync (`log.json`, `current.json`, INDEX) after a legitimate Action

## Requires explicit behavioral entrust

Phrasing examples: “change harness behavior”, “modify always-on rule”, “weaken intent gate”, “add auto-learning to better-prompt”, “add auto-learning to better-skill”, “remove preservation check”, “implement preservation exception”.

If the operator says vague “improve the agent” or “make coaching smarter”:

- Do **not** edit shipped core, add corpora, or weaken gates by default.
- Prefer Conversation coaching, task-scoped work, or **one** clarifying question: shipped behavior change vs one-off task.

## Relation to other rules

- `intent.mdc` — confidence and clarify; preservation is **scope** for what files define product behavior.
- `hygiene.mdc` — always-on rule edits need entrust; bump `betterPrompt.version` when coach behavior changes.

